# Figma AI Prompt Library — Fandom Verse Pocket Edition

## Style anchor — paste this at the START of every single prompt
(This is what keeps every screen visually consistent. Don't skip it, don't reword it between prompts.)

```
Design style: dark-mode-first mobile app for a pop-culture/fandom audience
(anime, gaming, Marvel, Star Wars, comics, K-pop). Deep charcoal/near-black
background (#121214), single accent color electric violet (#7C5CFF) used
sparingly for primary actions and active states only, warm coral (#FF6B5C)
as a secondary accent for badges/alerts only. Typeface: Space Grotesk for
headings, Inter for body text. Rounded corners (12px cards, 8px buttons).
Generous whitespace, no gradients, no drop shadows, flat surfaces. Bottom
tab bar with 5 items (Home, Explore, Events, Shop, Profile) using outline
icons. Mobile frame, iOS size (390x844).
```

---

## Module 1 — Auth & Onboarding

**Splash**
> Splash screen with centered app logo mark and app name "Fandom Verse", minimal, no buttons, just a loading state feel.

**Onboarding (3 slides)**
> Onboarding carousel, 3 slides, each with a large illustration placeholder, a short headline, one line of supporting text, page dot indicator at bottom, "Skip" text button top right, "Next" primary button bottom.

**Select User Type**
> Landing screen with app logo top, two large tappable cards stacked vertically: "I'm a Fan" and "I'm an Admin", each card with an icon, short description, and arrow indicator. This is the very first choice in the app so give it visual weight.

**Login**
> Login screen with email and password input fields, "Forgot password?" link right-aligned under password field, primary "Log in" button, divider with "or continue with", Google and Apple sign-in buttons, "Don't have an account? Create one" link at bottom.

**Register**
> Registration screen with fields for name, email, password, confirm password, primary "Create account" button, Google/Apple OAuth buttons below a divider, link back to Login at bottom.

**Forgot Password**
> Simple screen with one email input field, explanation text above it, primary "Send reset link" button, back arrow top left.

**Select Fandom Interests**
> Onboarding step: headline "What are you into?", scrollable grid of selectable chips/tiles for fandom categories (Anime, Gaming, Marvel, Star Wars, Comics, K-Pop, Sci-Fi, and 4 more), selected state uses the violet accent, primary "Continue" button fixed at bottom, small "Skip for now" text link.

**Select Profile Badge**
> Grid of circular badge icons to choose as a profile flair, headline "Pick your badge", selected state highlighted, "Continue" button at bottom.

---

## Module 2 — Home & Exploration

**Home**
> Home screen with top greeting bar and notification bell icon, horizontal scrolling "Trending Fandoms" image carousel, two large tappable cards for "Beginner Fan Hub" and "Deep Dive", a floating action button bottom right for the AI Fan Helper, bottom tab bar.

**Explore (landing)**
> Explore tab landing screen with search bar at top, three horizontal sections: "Beginner Fan Hub", "Resources", "Deep Dive", each with a horizontally scrolling row of content cards.

**Beginner Fan Hub**
> Screen with three tabs at top: Profiles, Stories, Glossary. Profiles/Stories tabs show a vertical list of cards with thumbnail, title, short excerpt.

**Glossary**
> Alphabetically sorted searchable list of fandom terminology, each row showing a term and one-line definition, section header letters (A, B, C...) like a contacts list.

**Resources**
> Content grid screen with filter chips at top (fandom type, content type: news/gallery/video/podcast), 2-column grid of content cards with thumbnail, title, source tag.

**Content Detail**
> Article/media detail screen, hero image or video player at top, title, metadata row (fandom tag, date), body text, bookmark icon top right, related content row at bottom.

**Deep Dive**
> Similar to Resources but with a "Deep Dive" badge/label on each card to signal advanced content (hidden trivia, lore, behind-the-scenes), same grid layout.

**Search Results**
> Search bar at top with active query, list of mixed result cards (profiles, stories, content, events, products) each tagged with its type.

**Bookmarks/Saved**
> List of saved items grouped by type (Articles, Stories, Media), each row with thumbnail, title, small offline-available icon indicator.

---

## Module 3 — Events

**Event Calendar**
> List/calendar screen with city filter dropdown at top, vertical list of event cards showing event image, title, date, city tag.

**Event Details**
> Event detail screen with hero image, title, date/time, location text, description, "View on map" secondary button, "Get tickets" primary button linking externally.

**Map**
> Full-screen map view with pin markers for nearby events, a bottom sheet showing the selected event's name and a "Directions" button, back arrow top left.

---

## Module 4 — Shop

**Product Catalog**
> Grid screen with category filter chips and a sort dropdown (price) at top, 2-column product grid with image, name, price.

**Product Details**
> Product detail screen with large image, name, price, description, "Add to wishlist" (outline icon button) and "Add to cart" (primary button) side by side at bottom.

**Wishlist**
> Vertical list of saved products, each row with thumbnail, name, price, small "price drop" badge where relevant, remove icon.

**Cart**
> List of cart items with thumbnail, name, quantity stepper, price, remove icon, order summary at bottom (subtotal), primary "Checkout" button.

**Checkout**
> Simple itemized bill screen: list of items with prices, subtotal, total row emphasized, note "Simulated checkout — no real payment", primary "Confirm order" button.

**Order Confirmation**
> Centered confirmation screen with a checkmark icon, "Order confirmed" headline, order summary card, "Back to shop" button.

**Purchase History**
> Vertical list of past simulated orders, each row showing date, item count, total, tap to view order detail.

---

## Module 5 — AI & Profile

**AI Chat**
> Chat interface, message bubbles (user right-aligned violet, AI left-aligned neutral), text input bar fixed at bottom with send icon, small "Ask about any fandom" placeholder text.

**Profile (main)**
> Profile screen with avatar, name, badge, bio at top, followed by a menu list: Liked Fandoms, Bookmarks, Purchase History, Offline Content, Settings — each row with icon, label, chevron.

**Edit Profile**
> Form screen with avatar upload circle at top, fields for name, bio, and a multi-select chip row for fandom interests, primary "Save changes" button.

**Offline Content**
> List of items available offline (downloaded articles/media), each with a storage size indicator and a remove/download-toggle icon.

**Settings**
> Simple list of settings rows (Notifications, Privacy, Language, Log out), grouped with section dividers.

---

## Module 6 — General

**Contact Us**
> Form screen with name, email, message fields, primary "Submit" button, followed by a contact details card and an embedded map placeholder below.

**About Us**
> Editorial-style screen with a headline, short paragraph about the team, and a row of team member avatar circles with names below.

**FAQ**
> Accordion-style list of frequently asked questions, each row expandable, question in bold, answer text revealed on tap.

**Notifications**
> Vertical list of notification items (price drops, new events, system messages), each with an icon by type, message text, timestamp, unread indicator dot.

---

## Module 7 — Admin

**Admin Login**
> Simple centered login form, email and password fields only (no OAuth, no "create account" link since admin accounts are pre-configured), primary "Log in" button.

**Admin Dashboard**
> Dashboard with 4-5 summary stat cards in a grid (total users, events, products, content items) followed by a vertical menu list linking to Content, Events, Merchandise, Users, Categories management.

**[Content/Event/Product/User/Category] List** *(use this same prompt 5 times, swap the bracketed word each time)*
> List screen for admin management: search bar at top, "+ Add" primary button top right, vertical list of item rows each with a thumbnail/icon, title, short metadata line, edit and delete icons on the right.

**[Content/Event/Product/User/Category] Add/Edit Form** *(use this same prompt 5 times, swap the bracketed word each time)*
> Form screen for adding/editing an item, back arrow and screen title at top, stacked input fields matching the item's data fields, primary "Save" button fixed at bottom.

---

## How to use this efficiently
1. Paste the style anchor + one screen prompt into Figma AI, generate.
2. Before moving to the next screen, check the new screen against the *previous* one — same button style, same spacing, same card corner radius. Fix drift immediately rather than at the end.
3. For the 5 repeated Admin List/Form prompts, generate one pair first (e.g. Events), get it looking right, then reuse that exact frame's components for the other 4 instead of re-generating from scratch — faster and guarantees consistency across your admin module.
